[11.714,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your Azure subscription (location northeurope); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. SSH key: the stack's own key pair, its public half handed to the template (.openvidu/azure/ov-e2ec-a105835-key.pub)\r\n  2. Template: render the single node template into .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-singlenode.bicep\r\n  3. Resource group: create ov-e2ec-a105835-rg in northeurope\r\n  4. Machines: Create the deployment ov-e2ec-a105835 with the machine, which installs OpenVidu Community on itself (about 4 minutes)\r\n  5. Wait for OpenVidu to answer, read the stack over SSH and register this directory as the stack\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on Azure…\r\n"]
[16.714,"o","   · create the resource group ov-e2ec-a105835-rg in northeurope\r\n"]
